From 131c9bb9366a7d5857c519792871cb89401fa2c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Illya Antonyuk <illantalex84@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:32:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/51] gpio: lpc32xx: allow on ARMv5 multiplatform without
 ARCH_LPC32XX

The PNX4008 has the same GPIO block (P3 GPIO/GPI/GPO banks at the same
offsets), but a PNX4008 board on the generic DT machine cannot enable
ARCH_LPC32XX. Allow the driver for ARCH_MULTI_V5 as well; it only
registers its chips at probe and writes no registers.

Tested on a Sony Ericsson P1i: GPO_21 (CAM_POW) is bit 21 of
P3_OUTP_SET/CLR/STATE, as on the LPC32xx.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpio/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/Kconfig b/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
index a01af1180..4cc058e9e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
@@ -392,7 +392,7 @@ config GPIO_LPC18XX
 
 config GPIO_LPC32XX
 	tristate "NXP LPC32XX GPIO support"
-	depends on OF_GPIO && (ARCH_LPC32XX || COMPILE_TEST)
+	depends on OF_GPIO && (ARCH_LPC32XX || ARCH_MULTI_V5 || COMPILE_TEST)
 	help
 	  Select this option to enable GPIO driver for
 	  NXP LPC32XX devices.
-- 
2.53.0

